{
  "dom_id": "step-q185152",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "What is the missing number?\n\n$28\\,\\times $\n{{field-1}}\n$%=7$",
  "worked_solution": "We can write the given problem as the following product:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%\\times 28=7\n$$\n\nUsing the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%=7÷28=\\frac{7}{28}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{28}=\\frac{7÷7}{28÷7}=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1\\times 25}{4\\times 25}=\\frac{25}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{25}{100}=25\\,%\n$$",
